  "result": "Perfect! All 181 tests pass. I've successfully implemented customer statements:\n\n**Created `src/statements.js`** with statement function:\n\n**`statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)`** returns:\n- `ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue })` on success\n- `CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND` for unknown customers\n\n**Filtering and processing:**\n- Normalizes customer ID (trim + uppercase)\n- Filters invoices for this customer only\n- Includes only 'issued' or 'partially_paid' statuses\n- Includes only invoices with issueDate on or before asOf\n- Sorts by issueDate ascending\n- Each invoice object includes:\n  - `number`: invoice number\n  - `issueDate`: issue date\n  - `dueDate`: payment due date\n  - `total`: invoice total (from invoiceTotals)\n  - `due`: amount still owed (from balanceDue)\n- `totalDue`: sum of all due amounts\n\n**Added 14 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- Unknown customer returns CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND\n- Empty list for customer with no invoices\n- Includes issued invoices in statement\n- Includes partially_paid invoices\n- Excludes draft invoices\n- Excludes paid invoices\n- Excludes invoices after asOf date\n- Includes invoices on asOf date (boundary case)\n- Due amounts for unpaid invoices\n- Due amounts for partially paid invoices\n- Correct sorting by issueDate\n- Correct totalDue calculation with tier discounts applied\n- Customer ID normalization (case/spaces)\n- Only includes current customer's invoices\n\nAll 181 tests pass (167 previous + 14 new). Customer statements are now fully functional and correctly aggregate outstanding invoice balances.",
